---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The loaded-mapper half of the `count()` guard (#973, #1014), and the third
# rule to say the same thing: `142` for a lambda, `143-count-keeps-elidable-
# named-map-native` for a `new Foo()`, this one for a mapper that arrives in a
# parameter, a local or a static field.
#
# The defect is `101`'s, verbatim. A `count()` that `101` did NOT stamp is one
# the JVM can elide: the source is SIZED, `map` preserves SIZED, and
# `ReferencePipeline.count()` answers from the spliterator without running the
# pipeline at all. `Stream.of(1, 2, 3).map(f).count()` therefore calls
# `f.apply` zero times; fuse the map into a `mapMulti`, which clears SIZED by
# design, and it is called once per element. Same specification, more work, and
# the fusion it buys optimises a pipeline that was never going to run.
#
# So the `invokeinterface Stream.map` is stamped `reverted ↦ Φ.true`.
# `215-recognize-ref-map` is closed on the four-binding opcode jeo emits, so a
# stamped one stops matching it, never becomes a Φ.hone.named-map, never folds
# into a distill, and the load in front of it is left where javac put it. jeo
# ignores the extra binding when assembling.
#
# Only the map needs it. A `filter(p)` clears SIZED whatever its argument is, so
# `101` stamps the terminal, `142` and both `143` rules stand down, and the
# filter fuses as it should.
#
# The load is bound but not read, and admitted for whatever it is: the guard
# here does not care which opcode pushed the mapper, only that the map ahead of
# an elidable `count()` is one no 2xx rule should lift. `215-recognize-ref-map`
# is the rule that decides which loads it can actually fuse.
#
# Closed on the unstamped opcode, so it cannot re-fire on its own output, and it
# runs after `102` has taken the own-line label out from between the load and
# the call.
name: count-keeps-elidable-ref-map-native
pattern: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-load ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-load-op,
      𝐵-load-operands
    ⟧,
    𝜏-map ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏6 ↦ "java/util/stream/Stream",
      𝜏7 ↦ "map",
      𝜏8 ↦ "(Ljava/util/function/Function;)Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
      𝜏9 ↦ Φ.true
    ⟧,
    𝐵-between,
    𝜏-count ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏-cclass ↦ 𝑒-cclass,
      𝜏-cmethod ↦ "count",
      𝜏-csignature ↦ "()J",
      𝜏-ciface ↦ 𝑒-ciface
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-load ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-load-op,
      𝐵-load-operands
    ⟧,
    𝜏-map ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏6 ↦ "java/util/stream/Stream",
      𝜏7 ↦ "map",
      𝜏8 ↦ "(Ljava/util/function/Function;)Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
      𝜏9 ↦ Φ.true,
      reverted ↦ Φ.true
    ⟧,
    𝐵-between,
    𝜏-count ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏-cclass ↦ 𝑒-cclass,
      𝜏-cmethod ↦ "count",
      𝜏-csignature ↦ "()J",
      𝜏-ciface ↦ 𝑒-ciface
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
when:
  or:
    - eq: [𝜏-load-op, 'aload']
    - eq: [𝜏-load-op, 'getstatic']
